qt0|n|A little face; a small, plane surface; as, the facets of a diamond. ; A smooth circumscribed surface; as, the articular facet of a bone. ; The narrow plane surface between flutings of a column. ; One of the numerous small eyes which make up the compound eyes of insects and crustaceans.	a:1067,46,3~1067,46,3
qt5|a|Given to wit and good humor; merry; sportive; jocular; as, a facetious companion. ; Characterized by wit and pleasantry; exciting laughter; as, a facetious story or reply.	j:pxn,51,1~pxn,51,1
qt9|a|Of or pertaining to the face; as, the facial artery, vein, or nerve.	j:3sv,159,7;qh4,113,11;wj2,105,7;1oil,101,8~qh4,113,11;1oil,101,8;3sv,159,7;wj2,105,7
qtd|a|Easy to be done or performed: not difficult; performable or attainable with little labor. ; Easy to be surmounted or removed; easily conquerable; readily mastered. ; Easy of access or converse; mild; courteous; not haughty, austere, or distant; affable; complaisant. ; Easily persuaded to good or bad; yielding; ductile to a fault; pliant; flexible. ; Ready; quick; expert; as, he is facile in expedients; he wields a facile pen.	e:22p7,55,4~22p7,55,4
qte|n|To make easy or less difficult; to free from difficulty or impediment; to lessen the labor of; as, to facilitate the execution of a task.	N:257f,36,1~257f,36,1
