r46|a|Conforming to the fashion or established mode; according with the prevailing form or style; as, a fashionable dress. ; Established or favored by custom or use; current; prevailing at a particular time; as, the fashionable philosophy; fashionable opinions. ; Observant of the fashion or customary mode; dressing or behaving according to the prevailing fashion; as, a fashionable man. ; Genteel; well-bred; as, fashionable society.	j:ro1,51,4~ro1,51,4	e:ha2,62,3;2753,30,5;1awf,16,3~2753,30,5;1awf,16,3;ha2,62,3
