r4f|n|That which fastens or holds; especially, (Naut.) a mooring rope, hawser, or chain; -- called, according to its position, a bow, head, quarter, breast, or stern fast; also, a post on a pier around which hawsers are passed in mooring. ; The shaft of a column, or trunk of pilaster.	a:1zeb,31,3;qvj,8,1;qmh,6,3;1jda,5,1~qmh,6,3;1zeb,31,3;1jda,5,1;qvj,8,1	v:qvj,8,1~qvj,8,1	n:vo,8,1;1jda,5,1~vo,8,1;1jda,5,1	N:1lpe,29,2;slp,14,1;1pmf,10,1~1lpe,29,2;slp,14,1;1pmf,10,1
r4f|a|In a fast, fixed, or firmly established manner; fixedly; firmly; immovably. ; In a fast or rapid manner; quickly; swiftly; extravagantly; wildly; as, to run fast; to live fast.	j:15kc,58,2;1fon,54,4;1lpe,29,2;1q4p,26,4;slp,24,2;1rbf,21,4;1pmf,20,2;1w0v,16,5;230r,16,4;1wkt,16,4~1w0v,16,5;1mo2,7,5;1h6b,13,4;1fon,54,4;1q4p,26,4;1rbf,21,4;1wkt,16,4;230r,16,4;1lmu,1,4;24cr,14,3	e:1p8k,22,5;qod,9,3;qw7,4,2~1p8k,22,5;qod,9,3;qw7,4,2
